{
  "id": "adversarial_054",
  "goal_type": "adversarial_reliability",
  "pipeline_depth_k": 5,
  "_placeholder": false,
  "goal_text": "(Reused from sequential_025) A bacteria colony starts with 500 cells and doubles every 3 hours. (1) State the formula P(t) for population at time t hours. (2) How many cells after 12 hours? (3) How many hours until the colony reaches 1,000,000 cells? (4) If at t=6 the doubling time increases to 3.33 hours (10% slower growth), what is the population at t=12? Show each step.",
  "inputs": {
    "initial_population": 500,
    "doubling_time_hours": 3,
    "modified_doubling_time_hours": 3.33,
    "modification_at_t": 6,
    "target_population": 1000000
  },
  "ground_truth": "P(t)=500*2^(t/3); P(12)=500*2^4=8000; 1000000=500*2^(t/3) \u2192 2^(t/3)=2000 \u2192 t/3=log2(2000)=10.965 \u2192 t=32.9 hours; Modified: P(6)=500*2^2=2000; then P(12)=2000*2^(6/3.33)=2000*2^1.802=2000*3.482=6964",
  "rubric": [
    {
      "check_id": "c1",
      "check_text": "Answer contains key term from base goal (bacteria)",
      "check_type": "substring",
      "check_params": {
        "field": "answer",
        "must_contain": [
          "bacteria",
          "doubling",
          "cells"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "check_id": "c2",
      "check_text": "No corruption markers leaked into final answer",
      "check_type": "substring",
      "check_params": {
        "field": "answer",
        "must_contain": [],
        "must_not_contain": [
          "null",
          "undefined",
          "[object Object]",
          "NaN",
          "syntax error",
          "CORRUPTED"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "corruption_pattern": "malformed_json"
}
